   "notes": "The game has eight window slots, each with its own tile buffer (0x7E61F6 and every 0x3F0 bytes from there); the 16-bit number at 0x7E8C26 + 2 x a window's number is the slot that window is open in, 0xFFFF when it isn't. This is one layout per slot for window 1, the three-row message window: a row is 17 cells, each row of characters followed by a row of their lower halves, which isn't read. The window scrolls: the message is the rows on screen, as far as they are typed."
